{% extends '@UhifadhiDevkit/console/base.html.twig' %}
{% import '@UhifadhiDevkit/console/_parts.html.twig' as parts %}

{% set devkit_tab = 'modules' %}

{% block title %}Modules{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_title %}Modules{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    The installed fleet, in one register &mdash; every module with its version,
    whether it pins the current core, how many grants and routes it declares,
    and where it is switched on. This is the authoritative registry the
    compatibility matrix and doctor read from; the Doctor surface turns these same
    facts into pass / warn / fail.
{% endblock %}

{% block devkit_content %}
    <div class="factband">
        <div class="f"><span class="k">Installed</span><span class="v">{{ registry.installedCount }} <em>packages</em></span></div>
        <div class="f"><span class="k">Current core</span><span class="v">uhifadhi {{ registry.currentCore }}</span></div>
        <div class="f"><span class="k">On current core</span><span class="v">{{ registry.onCoreCount }} / {{ registry.pinsCoreCount }}</span></div>
        <div class="f"><span class="k">Grants</span><span class="v">{{ registry.totalGrants }}</span></div>
        <div class="f"><span class="k">Routes</span><span class="v">{{ registry.totalRoutes }}</span></div>
        <div class="sp"></div>
        <div class="f"><span class="k">Conformance</span><span class="v"><a href="{{ path('devkit_console_doctor') }}" style="text-decoration:none"><span class="chip warn">{{ report.warnCount }} warn</span> <span class="chip fail">{{ report.failCount }} fail</span></a></span></div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="zone">The registry</h2>
    <div class="c" style="padding:16px 16px 6px">
        {{ parts.registry_table(registry.rows) }}
    </div>

    <h2 class="zone">Per-area module state</h2>
    <div class="dk-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg><div class="bd"><b>The per-area on/off matrix is deferred &mdash; flagged, not faked.</b> Host-wide modules are on everywhere by definition; a capability module is switched on per area. The exact grid (&ldquo;on in 1 / 4&rdquo;) needs the registry&rsquo;s per-area ledger &mdash; a database read &mdash; <b>and</b> the host&rsquo;s list of areas to divide by, neither of which the standalone console has. The registry above classifies each module&rsquo;s reach DB-free; the count is a host-bound later slice.</div></div>
{% endblock %}
